# The AIR of the crypt, on its own. NOT part of the building.
#
# void_crypt is what the manifest subtracts from the whole building: the air of this room less the
# stone this part puts back into it. For a room hollowed out of a solid podium that shape IS the
# room, so this is the probe to slice.
#
#   ./build/clipcheck clips/facility/requests/crypt-void-probe.clip --metre 16 --slice y@0.5
#   ./build/clipcheck clips/facility/requests/crypt-void-probe.clip --metre 16 --slice z@-8.5
#
# Anything in here that should have been STONE is a thing this part is about to lose to its own
# room: a grating, a taper, a sarcophagus or the stair. They are all in part_crypt, so none of them
# should show up in this shape.

include "../_contract.clip"
include "../_order.clip"

paint limestone

include "../crypt.clip"

# THE SAMPLED BOX IS CUT DOWN TO THIS ROOM, and that is the only reason a metre 32 run of it
# finishes. The contract's box is 34 x 20.9 x 25 m — 582 million cells at metre 32, nearly all of
# it the air over a building this fragment is 2.10 m underneath. This one is 24.6 x 3.1 x 15.8,
# which is 39 million, and it holds the whole room, both stairs, all three light-well corridors
# and the podium's top surface over them with a margin. A probe is not the building.
bounds -12.3 -0.95 -9.4   12.3 2.15 6.4

solid void_crypt
